  "upload": {
    "title": "How Does Amazon's Drone Know Where to Drop? 📦 #shorts",
    "description": "How does a delivery drone know where to drop your package? 📦\n\nAmazon's MK30 cruises high, then descends to about 4 meters (13 feet) above your yard. Its cameras and onboard perception scan the drop zone for people, pets, trampolines and clotheslines, and if anything is in the way, it doesn't drop: it looks for an alternative or flies away and tells you the delivery was attempted. It carries packages up to 5 pounds and delivers in under an hour.\n\nFaster than pizza, and politer than most couriers. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
